<!--Render Target Documentation — Presets
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.Presets-->
<rdoc:Presets xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Preset blocks to OpenSCAD customizer JSON
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A preset block (for example com.machineblocks.bml.bricks.StandardPresets
    with a _presets composition) may be rendered to an OpenSCAD customizer JSON
    file. The compiler merges appliedPresets chains before serialization.

    The JSON uses the preset name as the key (the label shown in the OpenSCAD UI):

        {
          "fileFormatVersion": "1",
          "parameterSets": {
            "Brick 2x4": {
              "size": "[2, 4, 3]",
              "baseColor": "#EAC645",
              "studs": "true"
            },
            "Brick 1x1": {
              "size": "[1, 1, 3]",
              "baseColor": "#EAC645"
            }
          }
        }

    All parameter values are strings (OpenSCAD customizer requirement). Emit
    only properties whose preset value differs from the block default. Omitted
    properties fall back to those defaults when OpenSCAD loads the parameter
    set.

    A block whose only composition is presets is rendered to the manifestation
    path with a .json suffix instead of a .scad file. basePresets chains are
    merged left to right, then the instance's own values overlay them. The
    parameter set key is the instance name. A basePresets cycle returns
    files: [] and diagnostic BML_PRESET_CYCLE.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:SourceMaps" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:Presets>
